      "title": "xml: Avoid copying elements unnecessarily",
      "message": "xml: Avoid copying elements unnecessarily\n\nduplicate_element is moderately expensive because it copies the maps\nof the element attributes and the pointer arrays of the element\nnames, among other things.\n\nRather than copying the pointer arrays and then freeing the copies\nafter use, just use the original pointer array, and iterate through it.\n\nWhen constructing a flat namesapce, the xml_ns_t for each element\nis used once, on the root_element. Rather than looking each element\nup in the map of all elements, copying it, and then later freeing\neach original element in the map of all elements, just remove them\nas they are used.\n\nWhen constructing a hiearchical namespace, we can use the original\nelement for the first level of recursion, and only do the expensive\ncopies on subsequent levels.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-08-03T07:44:55.000-04:00",
